## Summary

| Status | Count | Items |
|---|---|---|
| ✅ Fixed | 3 | #1, #2, #16 |
| 🔧 Recommended, not applied | 3 | #6, #7, #13 |
| 📝 Documented only | 11 | #3, #4, #5, #8, #9, #10, #11, #12, #14, #15, |

Every item was found either through direct code review of all 12 routers
and the schema, or through live debugging in the browser (specifically
#1, confirmed via DevTools Network tab showing a 72+ request loop). Fixes
were prioritized by risk: zero-risk, provably safe changes were applied
first (#1, #2, #17); changes requiring a product/policy decision beyond
what the code alone can answer were documented rather than guessed at
(#5, #8, #10); and the highest-risk architectural change (#15) was
deliberately left alone rather than attempted without enough time to
verify it thoroughly.

